PGC Schizophrenia Cognition: Genotype Protocol 

ID Matching 

The complete-case samples from each dataset (as generated using the Phenotype Protocol: https://github.com/eviedoherty/PGC_SCZ_Cognition_Protocol/tree/main)  should be matched to available PGC Wave 2, 3 and/or 4 genotype data on Snellius, the Dutch National Supercomputer.  

Sample size: Each dataset should have >100 individuals after matching phenotype to genotype IDs. 

Smaller datasets (<100): Datasets with <100 individuals will not be analysed in this iteration of the PGC SCZ – Cognition Subgroup analysis.  

However, you may still be able to contribute by combining several smaller datasets from the same cohort or ancestry. Please see the Data Preparation section for more details.  
